# Metrics

**Status:** Draft — founder review required
**Phase:** 7 — Operations (final file — completes the GrantAI roadmap)

## Purpose

Defines the rollup numbers that answer "is GrantAI actually working" at a
glance — what `ExecutiveGrantAdvisor-Agent` and the Monthly Routine in
`StandardOperatingProcedures.md` both surface.

## Core Metrics

**Volume**
- Opportunities discovered (by category, by source)
- Opportunities scoring High (70+) vs. Moderate vs. Low

**Pipeline**
- Drafts prepared (Hunter-triggered vs. on-demand)
- Reviewer pass rate
- Drafts reaching founder-review vs. stalling in revision

**Outcomes**
- Applications submitted (founder-confirmed, per `ApplicationTracker.md`)
- Win rate (awarded / submitted)
- Total funding pursued vs. total funding awarded

**System Health**
- Grant Hunter run success rate (per `AuditLogging.md` digests — did the
  scheduled sweep actually complete, and did it error on any source)
- Score-to-outcome correlation (are high-scored opportunities actually
  winning more — the core signal `ContinuousLearning.md` uses to
  recalibrate)

## What "Good" Looks Like

Not defined yet — deliberately. A target win rate or volume goal set before
a single real sweep has run would be a guess dressed up as a benchmark.
Recommend setting real targets after the first full quarter of data.

## This Completes the GrantAI Roadmap

All 7 phases are now drafted: Foundation, Agent Specifications, Knowledge
Base, Intelligence Engine, Application System, Engineering, and Operations.
The system is fully specified on paper — what's left is founder review of
the open decisions flagged throughout, activating real sources in
`FundingOrganizations.md`, and building the actual Supabase/Lovable
implementation per `docs/engineering/`.

